WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.597 --> 00:00:04.472
- Hey, I'm Courtney.

00:00:04.472 --> 00:00:05.390
- I'm Kevin.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:06.266
- I'm Stephanie.

00:00:06.266 --> 00:00:08.727
(Both laugh)
- And together.

00:00:08.727 --> 00:00:12.689
- (laughs) And together, we
are the chicken pot pie-ers.

00:00:13.148 --> 00:00:15.609
- Courtney is a chef, she's
also one of my best friends,

00:00:15.609 --> 00:00:17.527
and she's written so many cookbooks,

00:00:17.527 --> 00:00:19.654
worked in incredible famous kitchens,

00:00:19.654 --> 00:00:20.864
and we're so lucky to have her

00:00:20.864 --> 00:00:23.366
on the show making Elizabeth's food.

00:00:23.366 --> 00:00:24.910
- Let's begin, shall we?

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.704
(upbeat music)

00:00:29.748 --> 00:00:31.458
- I'm about to make the chicken pot pie

00:00:31.458 --> 00:00:33.210
with Kevin and Stephanie,

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.087
and this is a huge, huge dish on the show.

00:00:36.087 --> 00:00:37.505
- Yes.
- Without the chicken pot pie,

00:00:37.505 --> 00:00:38.840
you would not have "Supper at Six".

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.133
- That's right, it's the catalyst.

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:41.551
Kevin's character, Walter, takes a bite

00:00:41.551 --> 00:00:42.594
of this chicken pot pie,

00:00:42.594 --> 00:00:45.639
and it inspires him for
the rest of this series.

00:00:45.639 --> 00:00:47.057
- Yeah, and possibly life.

00:00:47.057 --> 00:00:48.934
- I would like to offer you a job

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:53.271
as the new host of RBLA
TV's latest cooking show.

00:00:53.271 --> 00:00:54.856
- Are you concussed?

00:00:54.856 --> 00:00:56.733
- But you know, I know Kevin a little bit,

00:00:56.733 --> 00:00:59.778
and he has said that
he is not a good cook,

00:00:59.778 --> 00:01:01.780
so I'm very excited to
see how this is gonna go,

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.950
because I think he's gonna
learn a lot from you today.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.868
- I also don't think Stephanie
is a huge cook either.

00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:08.495
- Oh, she's not?
- So I'm really curious

00:01:08.495 --> 00:01:09.454
to see how they do.

00:01:09.454 --> 00:01:11.831
- Hmm, I can't wait to find out.

00:01:11.831 --> 00:01:13.833
This is so fun!
- Me neither, me neither.

00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:16.920
(upbeat jazzy music)

00:01:18.755 --> 00:01:21.758
- I brought my chicken pot pie
recipe, along with a sample

00:01:21.758 --> 00:01:23.969
so that you can taste
the crumble of the crust

00:01:23.969 --> 00:01:25.345
and the viscosity of the filling.

00:01:25.345 --> 00:01:26.721
- Before we get started,

00:01:26.721 --> 00:01:29.224
please do tell me just a teensy little bit

00:01:29.224 --> 00:01:30.350
about your characters.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:31.643
- I play Fran Frask.

00:01:31.643 --> 00:01:34.938
I am the head of HR at Hastings Lab.

00:01:34.938 --> 00:01:37.440
Elizabeth and I bump heads a lot.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.484
- Since the day you got
here, you have just acted

00:01:39.484 --> 00:01:41.361
like you are so much
better than the rest of us,

00:01:41.361 --> 00:01:42.570
marching around these halls

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:43.863
with your perfect little nose up

00:01:43.863 --> 00:01:45.281
like you invented penicillin.

00:01:45.281 --> 00:01:46.783
- I play Walter.

00:01:46.783 --> 00:01:49.244
I am a producer at "Supper at Six".

00:01:49.244 --> 00:01:52.497
I also bump heads with
Elizabeth quite a bit.

00:01:52.497 --> 00:01:53.581
(laughs)

00:01:53.581 --> 00:01:55.458
- I hear your concerns.

00:01:55.458 --> 00:01:59.421
Thing is, TV, it needs
to be inviting and fun.

00:01:59.421 --> 00:02:02.382
- Cooking is not fun, it is vital work.

00:02:02.382 --> 00:02:03.967
- We're gonna start by making the filling.

00:02:03.967 --> 00:02:05.468
So we're gonna come over here,

00:02:05.468 --> 00:02:06.845
you're gonna dump the butter in.

00:02:06.845 --> 00:02:08.221
- Easy.

00:02:08.221 --> 00:02:09.055
Boom.
- Alright.

00:02:09.055 --> 00:02:10.682
- It's already sizzling.
- Yeah, it's sizzling.

00:02:10.682 --> 00:02:13.601
Now we're gonna add celery, carrots.

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:14.394
- Onions!

00:02:14.394 --> 00:02:17.689
- So, both of you, in the
show, you have big careers.

00:02:17.689 --> 00:02:19.315
What do you think it's like

00:02:19.315 --> 00:02:20.942
working with your character on the show?

00:02:20.942 --> 00:02:23.194
How do you contribute
to the work environment?

00:02:23.194 --> 00:02:23.945
- Hmm.

00:02:23.945 --> 00:02:29.075
- I play a TV producer, so
having been on a lot of TV sets,

00:02:29.075 --> 00:02:31.494
we're in a room with a
bunch of different people,

00:02:31.494 --> 00:02:33.538
and everybody brings
their own thing to it,

00:02:33.538 --> 00:02:35.915
especially, you know, actors.

00:02:35.915 --> 00:02:38.918
Most of them (laughs)
have something weird-

00:02:38.918 --> 00:02:40.879
- Yeah, kind of crazy.
- About them.

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:42.547
- I can relate to that right now.

00:02:42.547 --> 00:02:44.090
Deeply.
(laughs)

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.468
- With Fran, she's head of HR.

00:02:46.468 --> 00:02:50.889
She follows the rules, she
gets everybody excited to do-

00:02:50.889 --> 00:02:53.224
Ooh, we're adding in the
chicken, the shredded chicken.

00:02:53.224 --> 00:02:54.642
- But keep talking, you're doing great.

00:02:54.642 --> 00:02:56.102
- I mean, I can relate to her,

00:02:56.102 --> 00:02:58.354
because I think she tries to add a lot

00:02:58.354 --> 00:03:00.440
of fun to the workplace,

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.151
but she's a bit of a strict rule follower.

00:03:03.151 --> 00:03:04.486
- Yeah.
- Which can be

00:03:04.486 --> 00:03:05.528
probably obnoxious.

00:03:05.528 --> 00:03:08.031
- Are you a rule follower in real life?
- To some. 

00:03:08.031 --> 00:03:09.782
- Yeah.

00:03:09.782 --> 00:03:11.868
Yeah.
- Really, you're kind of like Fran?

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:14.704
Do you relate to Fran?
- More than I'd like to admit, yeah.

00:03:14.704 --> 00:03:15.830
- There is protocol, Miss Zott.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:18.374
When you don't follow
protocol, it falls on me.

00:03:18.374 --> 00:03:21.753
(mellow music)

00:03:21.753 --> 00:03:23.213
- You're just gonna do this,

00:03:23.213 --> 00:03:26.257
and the goal is you want
it to be pretty thin,

00:03:26.257 --> 00:03:27.258
about like this.

00:03:27.258 --> 00:03:28.635
I'm gonna place this here for now.

00:03:28.635 --> 00:03:30.428
Do you see the butter in here?

00:03:30.428 --> 00:03:32.639
- Oh, that's butter.
- So this is butter.

00:03:32.639 --> 00:03:35.308
That's what makes it really
flaky and crispy and delicious.

00:03:35.308 --> 00:03:36.643
Alright, you're doing great.

00:03:36.643 --> 00:03:37.936
- Lots of.
- Yeah.

00:03:37.936 --> 00:03:39.187
- Oh, it's, okay.
- Get the elbow grease.

00:03:39.187 --> 00:03:41.773
- So I’m not gonna have to do arms.

00:03:41.773 --> 00:03:43.149
- Yeah, you're just doing--
- Is it normal

00:03:43.149 --> 00:03:46.027
to throw out your back doing this?

00:03:46.027 --> 00:03:46.986
- Sometimes, yeah.

00:03:46.986 --> 00:03:48.488
- Uh-oh, wait, is that?

00:03:48.488 --> 00:03:49.405
- Alright, I'm gonna take this.

00:03:49.405 --> 00:03:50.990
- That is, like, so thin, brother.

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:52.951
- I know.
- Yeah, did I make it too thin?

00:03:52.951 --> 00:03:55.536
- No, I mean, well, maybe, but it's okay.

00:03:55.536 --> 00:03:56.412
It's gonna work.

00:03:56.412 --> 00:03:57.580
It's still gonna work great.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:58.831
(sighs)

00:03:58.831 --> 00:04:03.002
- I think that if I were gonna
make a dish for somebody,

00:04:03.002 --> 00:04:05.588
for like my husband, it
would be probably just

00:04:05.588 --> 00:04:07.173
like angel hair and basil.
- What kind of noodle?

00:04:07.173 --> 00:04:08.299
Angel hair?
- Yeah.

00:04:08.299 --> 00:04:09.133
- I love that.
- Or capellini.

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:10.343
- I like fusilli.

00:04:10.343 --> 00:04:11.177
- Fusilli?
- Yeah.

00:04:11.177 --> 00:04:12.428
- What's the difference there?

00:04:12.428 --> 00:04:13.263
- That's the--

00:04:13.263 --> 00:04:14.264
- The spirals?

00:04:14.264 --> 00:04:15.098
- Isn't that fusilli?

00:04:15.098 --> 00:04:17.433
- Yeah, I think the
point of the spirals is

00:04:17.433 --> 00:04:21.104
that the little bits of meat
go in the little grooves

00:04:21.104 --> 00:04:22.021
of the spiral.
- Ooh, yeah.

00:04:22.021 --> 00:04:24.482
- Yeah, I love fusilli, what can I say?

00:04:24.482 --> 00:04:27.527
- Did you see how well that I rolled this?

00:04:27.527 --> 00:04:29.737
- I know, it--
- I am a rule follower.

00:04:29.737 --> 00:04:31.239
- Yes.
- Like I said.

00:04:31.239 --> 00:04:33.825
- We have our dough, we have our filling,

00:04:33.825 --> 00:04:36.494
so we're each gonna assemble one.

00:04:36.494 --> 00:04:39.622
I'm just gonna cut a
square about this size

00:04:39.622 --> 00:04:40.790
to put in the bottom,

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:43.543
then I'm gonna cut round
like this for the top.

00:04:43.543 --> 00:04:45.753
Then you just put the
pie dough in the cup,

00:04:45.753 --> 00:04:46.713
push it into the bottom,

00:04:46.713 --> 00:04:48.756
make sure it goes all
the way to the edges.

00:04:48.756 --> 00:04:51.342
Trim it so there's just about,
I don't know, what is that?

00:04:51.342 --> 00:04:54.429
Half an inch of an overhang
all around the edge.

00:04:54.429 --> 00:04:55.430
Just like that.

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:56.472
So do y'all wanna do that?

00:04:56.472 --> 00:04:57.849
- Okay, we got the circle.

00:04:57.849 --> 00:04:58.683
- Circle.

00:04:58.683 --> 00:04:59.976
- Now we got the square.

00:04:59.976 --> 00:05:01.728
We're gonna place the square on top.

00:05:01.728 --> 00:05:02.979
- Yeah.
- There's nothing better

00:05:02.979 --> 00:05:06.107
