00:05:06.107 --> 00:05:07.191
- Mm-hmm, I agree.

00:05:07.191 --> 00:05:08.067
- Is that weird?

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:08.776
- No.

00:05:08.776 --> 00:05:11.696
- Would pie dough be the
same for like an actual pie,

00:05:11.696 --> 00:05:13.489
or would that be, like a dessert pie?

00:05:13.489 --> 00:05:16.492
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, so this
pie dough is very versatile.

00:05:16.492 --> 00:05:18.035
You can use it for savory,

00:05:18.035 --> 00:05:19.120
you could use it for dessert.
- Can I eat it?

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:19.912
- Yeah.

00:05:19.912 --> 00:05:21.414
It's literally just flour and butter, so.

00:05:21.414 --> 00:05:22.290
- It's really good.
- Yeah.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:24.500
- Oh, boy, I didn't think I
was gonna make it through that.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:25.501
- It looks great.
- You did it.

00:05:25.501 --> 00:05:26.335
- Thank you.

00:05:26.335 --> 00:05:28.921
- Okay, so now we're
just gonna fill these.

00:05:28.921 --> 00:05:30.381
Literally just get your spoon in there

00:05:30.381 --> 00:05:31.841
